# Working design/revision plans.  They are drafting notes that go stale against the code;
# what survives a plan belongs in docs/ and CHANGELOG.md, which are tracked.
PLAN*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendor / site-confidential data -- NEVER commit.
#
# Siemens gradient-system descriptor files (.asc) carry vendor hardware
# coefficients: the PNS/CNS response model and the forbidden acoustic-resonance
# frequencies and bandwidths.  They are not redistributable.
#
# seqcraft locates them at run time via the SEQCRAFT_ASC_DIR environment
# variable and never reads a path inside this repository.  Tests needing a real
# hardware model are marked `hardware` and skip with an explicit message when
# SEQCRAFT_ASC_DIR is unset; everything else uses the synthetic model in
# seqcraft.verify.hardware.synthetic_hw(), which is checked in and contains no
# vendor numbers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.asc
*.ASC
asc/
**/asc/
*.dsv
*.coeff
GradSys*
*GradSys*
*_GPA_*
Measperm*

# Scanner / scan data
*.dat
*.twix
*.ima
*.dcm
*.rda
*.mrd
*.h5
*.npz
*.json

# Generated sequences and sidecars.  Regenerate by running the notebooks.
*.seq
*.seq.json
*.bseq

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
.pixi/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
junit*.xml

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Docs
site/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Secrets / local environment.  SEQCRAFT_ASC_DIR points at vendor data, so a .env holding it
# must never be committed -- see the vendor block above.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Scratch
scratch/
tmp/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example outputs are NOT tracked.
#
# The notebooks in examples/ write their .seq, .seq.json sidecar and .npz trajectory into
# examples/seq/.  They are build products of the notebooks and they are large -- one spiral
# DTI sequence is 326 kB of .seq plus 238 kB of trajectory, and every recompile rewrites
# them, so tracking them puts a ~600 kB binary-ish diff in the history on each run.
#
# This means "the output did not change" is NOT checkable from git history.  What guards
# against silent output change instead is the test suite: tests/compiler/fidelity.py proves
# the compiled waveform equals the logic block at the union of their knots, and the
# invariants in CompiledSequence._verify (duration, per-axis m0 and m1, label addresses)
# run on every compile.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
examples/seq/
